# Homelab CI (Tekton/Kaniko) + local dev: resolve packages through the Nexus npm
# group -> npm-proxy -> https://registry.npmmirror.com, with a local cache in
# Nexus. Kills the pnpm-install network variance in the image build.
# Setup: infra/homelab/k8s/nexus/scripts/setup-npm-proxy.sh (w10n-config repo).
# Anonymous read is enabled, so no auth token here.
# NOTE: nexus.wiloon.com only resolves on the homelab LAN / wg tunnel; off-network
# clones must override `registry` (e.g. `pnpm install --registry=https://registry.npmmirror.com`).
registry=https://nexus.wiloon.com/repository/npm-group/
# The fetch-* settings below are for npm only (the `npm install -g pnpm` step in
# the Containerfile): pnpm 11+ reads just the registry/auth from .npmrc and takes
# its network settings from pnpm-workspace.yaml, which mirrors these values.
# Fail a stuck request fast and retry soon: with 10 retries backing off 1-10 min
# (and npm's default 5 min fetch-timeout), one hiccup at the start of
# `npm install -g pnpm` left the 2026-09-25 CI build idle for 20+ min until the
# pipeline timed out. Worst case now is ~6 x 60s + ~3 min of backoff.
fetch-timeout=60000
fetch-retries=5
fetch-retry-mintimeout=10000
fetch-retry-maxtimeout=60000
